{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1kokYjQaJxAfHG7q9SY", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I had to stop partway through: the device connection failed with `BrokenPipeError` on every call, including `observe` and `open_app`, so I could not finish the sweep and did not sign off.\n\n**Bugs filed (2, both confirmed by reproducing):**\n\n1. **Encrypt dialog, stale mismatch error.** After Password and Repeat password both read \"abc12\", the \"Password doesn't match\" error stayed under Password with the red icon, even though OK was enabled. It only cleared when I made the inputs mismatch and then matched them again.\n2. **Pasting a folder into itself succeeds silently.** Copying Alpha and pasting it inside Alpha created a nested `Alpha/Alpha` with no error. I deleted that nested folder afterwards.\n\n**Checked and passing:**\n- Search within a folder: case-insensitive matching, correct results per query, no results for an unmatched query, and results clear correctly.\n- New folder: empty and whitespace-only names are blocked, `/` is rejected as \"Invalid Name\", and a duplicate name shows an error toast.\n- New file: creates `Delta.txt` correctly.\n- Rename: empty name is blocked, `x/y.txt` is \"Invalid Name\", a duplicate name shows an error and does not overwrite, and a valid rename to `Gamma Two` persists and is findable in search.\n- Copy and paste: pasting into the same folder shows the conflict dialog and SKIP leaves the list unchanged. Copying `notes.txt` into Alpha worked.\n- Move: cutting `Delta.txt` into Beta worked, and the source folder's count updated.\n- Rotation: landscape and back to portrait kept the folder contents and search state.\n\n**Not covered:**\n- Long-name boundary input.\n- Moving a folder into its own subfolder.\n- Cut-paste within the same folder.\n- Encrypt with matching passphrases on a second file.\n- The search progressive-delivery behaviour under heavier load.\n\n**Unfiled observations:**\n- The duplicate-folder toast says \"File with same name already exists\", and the New Folder dialog clears the typed name after that failure.\n- A LeakCanary heap-dump screen appeared once, apparently from the debug build. I left it alone.\n\n**Test data I left on the device:**\n- `Delta.txt.aes` in AndroidQA/Amaze, created by the encrypt test.\n- A folder named `Gamma Two`, originally created as `Gamma`.\n- A copy of `notes.txt` in Alpha.\n- `Delta.txt` moved from Amaze into Beta.\n\nOnce the device connection is back, the remaining areas to run are the untested cases above."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 165, "cache_read_input_tokens": 354505, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 165}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5c05dcb2-2c15-48d6-ad4a-32b6af736160", "uuid": "546c16d6-ce7e-4146-8fc7-db49c589e4ce", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T22:58:56.073Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1kokEdEprahu2A1hMzM"}
